WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.170
A tone generator, also known as a toner probe,
traces a copper cable wire in a wall.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:12.330
This tool is a two-piece tool in which a tone
generator is connected to one end of a cable

00:00:12.330 --> 00:00:15.889
connection, and then a toner probe is connected
to the other end.

00:00:15.889 --> 00:00:18.560
A tone is generated when a connection is made.

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.780
If there is no tone, chances are there is
a problem with the cable.

00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:27.030
Tone generators are also used to find out
which cable is terminated in which spot in

00:00:27.030 --> 00:00:31.660
a 110 block, which is a necessary task if
the cables are not properly labeled in the

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.010
first place.

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:37.460
This particular process, as you can imagine,
can be rather laborious.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:42.130
One time, I needed to use this tool to figure
out which of five dangling cables from a ceiling

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:44.480
was connected to a server in another room.

00:00:44.480 --> 00:00:48.660
I had the probe in one hand and a cell phone
in the other with a coworker that let me know

00:00:48.660 --> 00:00:50.670
when a tone was generated.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:51.670
Wouldn't you know it?

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:55.480
I forgot the labeler, so I had to run down,
get that, and verify this again.

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:57.329
It pays to plan when troubleshooting.

